WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.452
What makes an AI agent work well?

00:00:02.452 --> 00:00:04.468
AgentSpec lets us test its parts.

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:10.928
Standard interfaces connect five modules, so we can change one
while keeping the others fixed.

00:00:11.433 --> 00:00:15.129
Perception turns observations into a usable state.

00:00:15.633 --> 00:00:18.297
Memory brings back relevant experience.

00:00:18.800 --> 00:00:21.776
Reasoning uses that information to propose a plan.

00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:25.660
Reflection checks the plan and suggests improvements.

00:00:26.167 --> 00:00:27.378
Action executes it.

00:00:27.378 --> 00:00:30.607
The environment returns feedback for the next step.

00:00:31.133 --> 00:00:34.373
This shared loop makes controlled comparisons possible.

00:00:34.900 --> 00:00:41.116
We can swap the model, memory, reasoning method, or reflection
strategy, and measure what changes.

00:00:41.633 --> 00:00:48.521
The same framework supports delivery planning, household tasks,
grid navigation, and three-dimensional environments.

00:00:49.033 --> 00:00:51.846
Each line here is a module combination.

00:00:51.846 --> 00:00:54.256
Higher means more profit on DeliveryBench.

00:00:54.256 --> 00:00:58.273
The agent's design changes how well the underlying model
performs.

00:00:58.800 --> 00:01:01.672
This heatmap pairs reasoning methods with different memories.

00:01:01.672 --> 00:01:03.467
Darker cells mean higher profit.

00:01:03.467 --> 00:01:07.416
The best memory depends on the reasoning method it works with.

00:01:07.933 --> 00:01:09.910
The orange bars add self-refinement.

00:01:09.910 --> 00:01:15.445
Every configuration shown earns more profit when it checks and
revises its own plan.

00:01:15.967 --> 00:01:18.509
Training also interacts with the modules.

00:01:18.509 --> 00:01:25.711
The green method, SUPO, learns to summarize history and works
especially well with the starred memory combinations.

00:01:26.233 --> 00:01:32.521
AgentSpec helps us study which components work together, and
build better agents through controlled experiments.
